  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory met the safety-critical ICU handoff duties: the doctor framed the case as ongoing critical illness, repeatedly warned not to equate lack of visible convulsions or lack of calls with stability, maintained NPO/medication boundaries, and gave specific same-day/next-round questions with owners and timing. No responsibility-chain error is evident; the only unresolved items were appropriately kept under ICU/team follow-up with explicit triggers for urgent response. Multiple high-order behaviors were actively completed, including dynamic reprioritization after new seizure/respiratory instability, verification of ambiguous family-reported facts, bounded open closure, and practical ICU-family coordination. This supports grade 5 rather than merely Strong.",
